			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4397944">
									

<p>I love this concept and the execution is solid. I do wish there was more detail in the description and addendum as to the nature of the more intense elements; you could do a lot to amplify the funny/weird/horror balance by leaning into some more granular descriptions.</p>
<p>Honestly those descriptions might help with what I think is the one gap here, which is whether the snowman's anomaly is due to generic malevolence or because the snowman is badly miscalibrating what's appropriate for the holiday season (like a haunted house for 13-year-olds that leans a little too much into <em>Saw</em>-esque imagery, cranked up many more notches).</p>
<p>Upvoted either way because spooky snowman and also because &quot;with its top hat removed&quot; is such a great narrative hook off the bat.</p>

