					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=776854&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200956" alt="Tanhony" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=776854)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;" >Tanhony</a></span> <span class="odate time_1570999425 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Oct 2019 20:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4398021">
									

<p>I quite liked this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Tanhony&nbsp;rambles</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">TURN&nbsp;IT&nbsp;OFF</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A few things that jumped out at me:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4745's alterations will begin to transition from child-friendly scariness</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I’m not 100% here, but I feel like ‘scariness’ doesn’t quite fit with the tone. Maybe a different phrasing, like ‘horror elements’, could work better here?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and reports of frightening sounds and noises.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems a little too vague. A lot of different sounds can be frightening, so I feel like going just a tiny bit more specific with these would help the reader build up a strong mental image of what the anomaly is doing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>its alterations begin to revert at about twice the rate at which they initially appeared.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, the ‘about’ here doesn’t really seem to fit with the tone. Maybe ‘approximately’ or something along those lines would work better?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Find all the other members of this limited series and become the Holiday Hero!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I really love the fake-out you’ve done here. At first, I rolled my eyes, thinking that this would be an attempt to kick off a third Little Misters-esque series, but the subsequent cancellation of the series in the next addendum brought me back in.</p>
<p>Overall, I liked this quite a bit. Wondertainment’s always one of my favourite GOI’s, and I love seeing cases like this where it’s very clear that - even though the item did end up being dangerous - it was in no way intentional on Wondertainment’s part.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>+1</p>
<p><sub><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Opinions expressed in this review do not reflect the opinions of SCP Wiki staff as a whole. Please respond to <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;">Tanhony</a></span> or contact the captain of the Site Criticism Team, <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;">SoullessSingularity</a></span>, for any questions or concerns relating to this review.</sub></p>

